## 3. Twisted-Morita cancellation

### Lemma 3.1

The maps

```text
Ad(G_ij):B_j -> B_i
```

form an honest Cech cocycle of graded algebra automorphisms.

### Proof

On a triple overlap,

```text
Ad(G_ij) Ad(G_jk) Ad(G_ki)
 =Ad(alpha_ijk I)
 =id.
```

Moreover,

```text
Ad(G)(XY)=Ad(G)(X) Ad(G)(Y),
```

and evenness of `G` preserves the grading. Therefore the local endomorphism
algebras glue to an ordinary sheaf of graded algebras even when the fundamental
module does not. QED.

### Lemma 3.2

The curvature and curved differential glue:

```text
F_i=Ad(G_ij)F_j,
d_i Ad(G_ij)=Ad(G_ij)d_j.
```

### Proof

The first identity follows by squaring the supercharge relation. For homogeneous
`X`, insert `q_i=G_ij q_j G_ij^(-1)` into the graded commutator. The two terms
factor by conjugation with the same sign because `G_ij` is even. QED.

This proof does not require `q_i` or `F_i` to commute with the projective
action. In fact, the exact witness below deliberately makes them non-invariant.

